# Build context for guardmatch-ai.
#
# The context is this directory, not the repository root, so anything at the root
# is already outside it — the Makefile, docker-compose.yml, .github/, .git/,
# PLAN.md and PROGRESS.md cannot reach this image and are not listed. Rules for
# paths that cannot exist here read as protection and provide none.
#
# What *is* listed falls into two groups, and the difference matters.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Present, and deliberately excluded
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Regenerable from a seed via `guardmatch generate-data`. ~5.7 MB that the image
# has no use for: the service scores what it is sent, it does not read the
# training set.
data/

# The suite runs in CI and locally, never inside the runtime image. An image that
# carries its own tests carries code it will never execute.
tests/
notebooks/

# Caches and build leftovers. Copying a host cache into a Linux image at best
# wastes layers and at worst confuses a tool into trusting a stale result.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
coverage.xml
*.egg-info/

# Read by the builder before the context is sent, so shipping them is redundant.
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Absent today, and must stay absent — kept precisely because they match nothing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These are the accident-prevention rules. `.env.example` is committed and holds
# no values; a real `.env` holds all of them, and the difference between the two
# filenames is one keystroke. A secret baked into an image layer stays in that
# layer even after a later layer deletes it, so this list earns its place long
# after it stops matching anything.
#
# No exception is needed for `.env.example`: the Dockerfile never copies it.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
id_rsa*

# A host virtualenv contains Windows-built binaries that cannot run in the image,
# and it is large enough to double the context.
.venv/
venv/
htmlcov/
build/
dist/

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
